1. Wheel Count, Function & Swappability (3 to 6 Wheels): Cars must run 3, 4, 5, or 6 wheels. Every wheel must actively contribute to steering or stabilization and must be externally accessible and swappable during a pit stop (banning hidden retractable "landing gear" wheels).
2. Ground Contact ("Airtime" Clause): At least one wheel must remain in contact with the track at all times, except when catching unintentional airtime off track bumps, kerbs, or crests.
3. Dimensional Box: Cars must fit within existing maximum length and width limits so no car can physically block the track.
4. Open Clean Propulsion & Zero Hazardous Materials (<60% Electric): Any powertrain architecture is permitted as long as electric motors provide less than 60% of total power (no 100%-torque-at-0-RPM EV dominance), zero harmful exhaust gases are emitted, and all radioactive materials (including depleted uranium ballast) or unsafe chemical reactions are strictly prohibited anywhere on the car.
5. Open Global Materials (No Export-Restricted / Exclusive Alloys): Every material used in the car's construction must be commercially available to all competing teams worldwide without national export bans, defense classifications, or single-manufacturer exclusivity.
6. Cockpit Canopy Freedom & Default Safety/Weight: Teams may build either an open cockpit (with Halo protection) or a closed fighter-jet style canopy (meeting rapid-extraction safety standards). Standard FIA survival cells, crash structures, fire suppression, and minimum weight rules remain mandatory.
7. Total Design Freedom: Everything outside Rules 1–6 (active aero, fan cars, active suspension, custom layouts) is 100% unrestricted.
